  "question": "If $\\cos^{-1}x=\\sin^{-1}y$, then $x=$?",
  "answeroption": "C",
  "explanation": "Let $\\theta=\\cos^{-1}x=\\sin^{-1}y$.<br /><br />Then $\\cos\\theta=x$ and $\\sin\\theta=y$.<br /><br />Using $\\sin^2\\theta+\\cos^2\\theta=1$, we get $x^2+y^2=1$.<br /><br />Thus $x=\\sqrt{1-y^2}$.",
